# Hollow Reach: an interconnected-map exploration platformer invented as a genre example. No
# game's names, data or logic. One large map in five zones, joined both ways; movement
# abilities open new parts of it, so a player keeps coming back to rooms seen earlier. Each
# zone is its own file, as a world this size would be split.
world hollow_reach "Hollow Reach" version 1
use items
use logic
use zones/surface
use zones/caverns
use zones/archive
use zones/spire
use zones/core
start landing_site

# How much the logic trusts the player's movement skill. `basic` and `advanced` count known
# tricks (a dash-jump across a gap, a climb without wall claws) as ways through.
option tricks: choice(none, basic, advanced) = none
# How many of the three zone guardians must fall before the core opens.
option guardians_needed: range 1..3 = 3
# Start with the dash, for shorter seeds.
option start_dash: toggle = off

start_item rush_core when opt.start_dash

goal core_silenced
